{
  "_comment": [
    "The trajectory calculation both backends must implement alike (docs/CONTEXT.md §Calculation",
    "spec, BOOTSTRAP.md §6, issue #73). Both suites read this file; neither keeps a copy of the",
    "numbers.",
    "`parameters`: the fixture-wide defaults. `warm_up_days` pins State to afloat while",
    "days_elapsed < warm_up_days. `drifting_below` and `taking_on_water_below` are dimensionless",
    "multipliers of the Baseline Daily Budget (B): State compares Trajectory Variance (V) against",
    "threshold x B directly, with no division, so a non-terminating B never enters the comparison",
    "as a rounded number. Any `figures` row may override any of the three via its own",
    "`warm_up_days` / `drifting_below` / `taking_on_water_below` fields.",
    "`figures` rows: symbols follow CONTEXT.md's table (P=daily_pool, D=period_days,",
    "e=days_elapsed, S_settled=settled_spend, S_today=today_spend, S_future=future_spend). Every",
    "money figure is a 4dp string. `forward_daily_rate` is null exactly when r = D - e = 1 (the",
    "last day of the Period), per CONTEXT's 'undefined on the last day' rule. Every allowance",
    "figure (baseline_daily_budget, todays_allowance, forward_daily_rate) is floored toward -inf at",
    "4dp (R1); left_to_spend_today is floored A minus the exact S_today, never independently",
    "rounded. trajectory_variance and buffer_days go on the wire half-up (half away from zero) at",
    "4dp (R2), computed from exact values, never from another figure's rounded output.",
    "`target_line` rows: the mid-period Budget change from CONTEXT §Mid-period Budget changes.",
    "`effective_day` is 1-indexed (`j`); T(j-1) is the cumulative target through day j-1 under the",
    "old baseline. `expected.targets` lists the cumulative target at specific days, half-up at 4dp;",
    "`expected.baseline_after` is the new baseline (B_new), floored at 4dp, and may be zero or",
    "negative when the clamp engages (P_new <= T(j-1)) - the target line itself stays flat at",
    "T(j-1) for the rest of the Period in that case, never dipping below it.",
    "Every expected value here was computed independently in exact rational arithmetic (Python's",
    "fractions.Fraction) and cross-checked against Python's decimal module with ROUND_FLOOR /",
    "ROUND_HALF_UP, not derived from either backend's implementation."
  ],
